  "selection": "36<=lat<41, -92<=lon<-86; archive event count>=25; one station nearest each 1 degree cell centre across TA/XO11; network/station tie break",
  "southwest": "All five previously identified San Juan/Zuni stations; development, not blind external validation",
  "qc": "Archived gaussian2.5 iterative RF match>=80, .04<=p<=.085. All three components available/aligned. Vertical P-window RMS[-1,9]/pre-P RMS[-10,-3]>=3. For every band normalized radial P amplitude>0.03 and abs RF<=8. No waveform fit to an inverted model used.",
  "processing": "Remove mean and linear trend, cosine taper5%; downsample waveform components to5Hz; rotate N/E using archived baz; common [-10,70]s P window. Spectral water-level deconvolution 1e-4, nfft2048, genuine Gaussian widths1/2.5/4. Radial and reference vertical use same spectral denominator and vertical peak normalization. Preserve raw RF and P-normalized RF separately.",
  "split": "After waveform QC: three equal-count slowness bins; sort event origin within bin, every fourth held out; >=6 training and>=2 test events/bin. Original southwest development labels are not claimed as independent confirmation.",
  "common_target": "Original-program comparison uses the middle slowness bin, actual raw gaussian2.5 RF stack, one mean ray, training SEM plus .02-amplitude discrepancy. Same physical likelihood/prior for all three samplers.",
  "full_target": "Three ray bins and three bands, raw RF stacks and training-only shrunk covariance; three quadrature rays/bin. Flow receives genuine P-normalized nine channels; it supplies candidates only.",
  "assessment": "All selected/excluded stations and reasons retained. Held-out events never used for candidate selection, optimization, noise estimation or stopping. RF predictive quality is not a known geological truth.",
